# Receiving Label improve loop — CONTINUE UNPROMPTED (training)

When this agent (or any concurrent agent) touches Receiving Label PDF/layout
(`buildReceiving` / `_drawReceivingPage`), **own the improve loop**. Do not stop
after one tweak and wait for the user to re-ask. This loop **trains** Receiving
layout quality over time.

## Mandatory loop

1. Read `qa_receiving/synthetic/improve_summary_latest.json` (create/run if missing).
2. Fix real **top_failures** / gate fails (long-field cutoff, logo/Swift
   encroachment, missing yellow SO pill, missing SO→PM hairline, missing
   received band, wrong instructions alert).
3. Re-run: `python scripts/receiving_label_improve_loop.py` from repo root.
4. Confirm mean composite and gates move the right way; iterate if clear
   score-proven bugs remain.
5. Append lessons to `qa_receiving/synthetic/training_lessons.json`; expand cases
   when new Receiving failure modes appear.

Docs: `qa_receiving/synthetic/README.md`. See also `improve-loops-training.mdc`.

## Receiving vs Shipping (do not confuse)

| Behavior | Receiving | Shipping (locked) |
|---|---|---|
| Under-pill `showRule` | **true** (SO → PM) | **false** |
| SO pill color | Yellow `recvSoBg` | Peach `soBg` |
| Layout | Full-width stack | Two-column |

Never “fix” Receiving by forcing Shipping’s `showRule: false`. Never edit
Shipping’s approved SO/Contact constants (`afterPillGap` 11.0, Contact 3.0) as a
side effect of Receiving work.

## North star

- Matrix case `baseline_receiving_sample` (`ShippingLabelData.receivingSample`)
- Visual anchors: RECEIVING chip, yellow SO pill + hairline, PM, received band,
  orange bumpers, red instructions alert when non-empty

## Out of scope for “fixes”

- Do not loosen harness soft gates to hide a regression.
- Do not commit/push unless the user asked. The improve loop itself does not
  require a commit.
